{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-263855" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $P(A)=0.55,$ $P(B)=0.35,$ and $P(A\\cap B)=0.15,$ find $P({A}^{′}\\cap {B}^{′}).$\n\n$P({A}^{′}\\cap {B}^{′})=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/state.json" "file_sha256" "e68717936bd031d5cfb04580bbe25be74a3e32a5bf1d18a9520f1fe92863851a"} {"question" "q-263855" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate $P(A\\cup B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\  & =0.55+0.35-0.15 \\\\  & =0.75\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we construct the corresponding Venn diagram and shade the region ${A}^{′}\\cap {B}^{′}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/e71239d41a4317c2c7c7015ee2947266075864cec768161fdc4874e8b48f5056.png)\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nP({A}^{′}\\cap {B}^{′})=0.25.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/state.json" "file_sha256" "e68717936bd031d5cfb04580bbe25be74a3e32a5bf1d18a9520f1fe92863851a"} {"question" "q-263855" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4a414690e6e50037ea09c3d4dc9545c576a8c81540fafb44a526ed48adab5928"} {"question" "q-263855" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/state.json" "file_sha256" "e68717936bd031d5cfb04580bbe25be74a3e32a5bf1d18a9520f1fe92863851a"} {"question" "q-263855" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.25"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/state.json" "file_sha256" "e68717936bd031d5cfb04580bbe25be74a3e32a5bf1d18a9520f1fe92863851a"} {"question" "q-246758" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $P(A)=0.4,$ $P(B)=0.5,$ and $P(A\\cap B)=0.2,$ find $P(A\\cap {B}^{′}).$\n\n$P(A\\cap {B}^{′})=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/state.json" "file_sha256" "e68717936bd031d5cfb04580bbe25be74a3e32a5bf1d18a9520f1fe92863851a"} {"question" "q-246758" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate $P(A\\cup B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\  & =0.4+0.5-0.2 \\\\  & =0.7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we construct the corresponding Venn diagram and shade the region $A\\cap {B}^{′}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/52a7c0ed9285d2699087f0ef817257eacebfabd5cfb2117167730a66b94da3e6.png)\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nP(A\\cap {B}^{′})=0.2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/state.json" "file_sha256" "e68717936bd031d5cfb04580bbe25be74a3e32a5bf1d18a9520f1fe92863851a"} {"question" "q-246758" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4a414690e6e50037ea09c3d4dc9545c576a8c81540fafb44a526ed48adab5928"} {"question" "q-246758" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/state.json" "file_sha256" "e68717936bd031d5cfb04580bbe25be74a3e32a5bf1d18a9520f1fe92863851a"} {"question" "q-246758" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/state.json" "file_sha256" "e68717936bd031d5cfb04580bbe25be74a3e32a5bf1d18a9520f1fe92863851a"} {"question" "q-263853" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $P(A)=0.5,$ $P(A\\cap B)=0.2,$ and $P(A\\cup B)=0.85,$ find $P({A}^{′}\\cap B).$\n\n$P({A}^{′}\\cap B)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/state.json" "file_sha256" "e68717936bd031d5cfb04580bbe25be74a3e32a5bf1d18a9520f1fe92863851a"} {"question" "q-263853" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate $P(B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ 0.85 & =0.5+P(B)-0.2 \\\\ P(B) & =0.85-0.5+0.2 \\\\ P(B) & =0.55\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we construct the corresponding Venn diagram and shade the region ${A}^{′}\\cap B.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/43267ee39b162c12235739ea84e9be539015ea28627caf14828b5fb5cc9fcd7b.png)\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nP({A}^{′}\\cap B)=0.35.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/state.json" "file_sha256" "e68717936bd031d5cfb04580bbe25be74a3e32a5bf1d18a9520f1fe92863851a"} {"question" "q-263853" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4a414690e6e50037ea09c3d4dc9545c576a8c81540fafb44a526ed48adab5928"} {"question" "q-263853" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/state.json" "file_sha256" "e68717936bd031d5cfb04580bbe25be74a3e32a5bf1d18a9520f1fe92863851a"} {"question" "q-263853" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.35"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/state.json" "file_sha256" "e68717936bd031d5cfb04580bbe25be74a3e32a5bf1d18a9520f1fe92863851a"} {"question" "q-179490" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $P(B)=\\frac{11}{20},$ $P(A\\cap B)=\\frac{1}{4},$ and $P(A\\cup B)=\\frac{3}{4},$ find $P({A}^{′}\\cap B).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/state.json" "file_sha256" "e68717936bd031d5cfb04580bbe25be74a3e32a5bf1d18a9520f1fe92863851a"} {"question" "q-179490" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate $P(A)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ \\frac{3}{4} & =P(A)+\\frac{11}{20}-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ P(A) & =\\frac{3}{4}-\\frac{11}{20}+\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ P(A) & =\\frac{15}{20}-\\frac{11}{20}+\\frac{5}{20} \\\\ P(A) & =\\frac{9}{20}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we construct the corresponding Venn diagram and shade the region ${A}^{′}\\cap B.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/b39a37400a7831f642cd6fe1d71db3c518fd348531a09ebc9d601586ed44afa5.png)\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nP({A}^{′}\\cap B)=\\frac{3}{10}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/state.json" "file_sha256" "e68717936bd031d5cfb04580bbe25be74a3e32a5bf1d18a9520f1fe92863851a"} {"question" "q-179490" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficu