{5}{12}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{12}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/state.json" "file_sha256" "e68717936bd031d5cfb04580bbe25be74a3e32a5bf1d18a9520f1fe92863851a"} {"question" "q-179529" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7}{12}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/state.json" "file_sha256" "e68717936bd031d5cfb04580bbe25be74a3e32a5bf1d18a9520f1fe92863851a"} {"question" "e-13034" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/ca3ae8f8df5bb20c40261cb25dbfdcf31a71717c01b6ef820c5c5ded2aedbbfc.png), ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/6071a2687c038fe8b7e95abe89c07b93aebe21424fadde72eb5ac52e64771895.png), ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/6a2c9b8bfdd3b9c0f642c1a96f8914926a2ef7c2f0aacdc536cee42760a63448.png), find ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/7ca88e3705a778b7a8329a2a7ae3248a377a79aa2a88bee51e7360dd36536e82.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/example-13034.json" "file_sha256" "a6cbd1465f66ccfd817a9d5f3c466769e1315ceddedcbe44ec85474ac4b19daa"} {"question" "e-13034" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/9b7b7cbb7f22bed24e5dafdfdbb4e29cc434eaeeb361ac601673654299dfedd0.png) using the addition law\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/8ac1b158770eacf57e651320b9aff02492fa6693383cd5c07c43fbcf439a3141.png)\n\nThen, we construct the corresponding Venn diagram and shade the region ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/8951b2f0456d6317f684dba75a4eb098bfeeb6fa77ec83947d4e2f09baadaece.png)\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/bac5655a5b79a32e8155e26be50275409a6bbf41b939cfb823e5e53fccef6663.png)\n\nFinally, we have\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/dc3c94937b19dc1efda8aa5356c0985fc6833d85cdfa1437a5fc60c88e018de9.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/example-13034.json" "file_sha256" "a6cbd1465f66ccfd817a9d5f3c466769e1315ceddedcbe44ec85474ac4b19daa"} {"question" "e-12933" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $P(A)=\\dfrac12,$ $P(A \\cap B)=\\dfrac16,$ and $P(A \\cup B)=\\dfrac23,$ find $P(A'\\cup B').$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/example-12933.json" "file_sha256" "8a3f8d8cd3d0b0b383414ae1789968188bdcce3dd76e7633375e13b6c51241ec"} {"question" "e-12933" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate $P(B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}+P(B)-\\frac{1}{6} \\\\ P(B) & =\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ P(B) & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we construct the corresponding Venn diagram and shade the region $A'\\cup B'.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/9856c9b0fdf3bf4b8f84417f6e625d823590f57dac4dcc8185994aef3f8c5e50.png)\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nP(A'\\cup B') = \\dfrac1{3} + \\dfrac{1}{6} + \\dfrac{1}{3} = \\dfrac56.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/example-12933.json" "file_sha256" "8a3f8d8cd3d0b0b383414ae1789968188bdcce3dd76e7633375e13b6c51241ec"} {"question" "e-13035" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $P(B)=0.6,$ $P(A\\cap B)=0.4,$ and $P(A\\cup B)=0.9,$ find $P(A').$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/example-13035.json" "file_sha256" "9f86f2140c805123d2b974c9d53aa87b0c8a8b11d50f1d039e1891a58d091e03"} {"question" "e-13035" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate $P(A)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ 0.9 & =P(A)+0.6-0.4 \\\\ P(A) & =0.9+0.4-0.6 \\\\ P(A) & =0.7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({A}^{′}) & =1-P(A) \\\\  & =1-0.7 \\\\  & =0.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/example-13035.json" "file_sha256" "9f86f2140c805123d2b974c9d53aa87b0c8a8b11d50f1d039e1891a58d091e03"}] "usage" {"e-12933" [] "q-264077" [] "e-13035" [] "e-13034" []} "basis" 1499 "retractions" [[17592186198867 :question/problem "Given that $P(A) = \\frac{1}{4}$, $P(B) = \\frac{1}{6}$, and $P(A∩B) = \\frac{1}{12}$, find $P(A^{′}∪B)$. Do not round your answer.$P(A^{′}∪B) =$\n{{field-1}}"] [17592186198067 :question/problem "Given $P(A)=0.3$, $P(B)=0.5$, and $P(A\\cup B)=0.7$, find $P(A'\\cap B)$."] [17592186198067 :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $P(A\\cap B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(A∪B) &= P(A) + P(B) - P(A∩B) \\\\\n0.7 &= 0.3 + 0.5 - P(A∩B) \\\\\nP(A∩B) &= 0.3 + 0.5 - 0.7 \\\\\nP(A∩B) &= 0.1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we construct the corresponding Venn diagram and shade the region $A'\\cap B$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/4315/Source/Images/cb945eebe175b9cf96e1be4d308d32d0.png)\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nP(A'\\cap B) = 0.4\n$$"] [17592186198057 :question/problem "Given that $P(A)=\\dfrac12$, $P(A \\cap B)=\\dfrac16$, and $P(A \\cup B)=\\dfrac23$, find $P(A'\\cup B')$."] [17592186198057 :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $P(B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(A∪B) &= P(A) + P(B) - P(A∩B) \\\\\n\\frac{2}{3} &= \\frac{1}{2} + P(B) - \\frac{1}{6} \\\\\nP(B) &= \\frac{2}{3} + \\frac{1}{6} - \\frac{1}{2} \\\\\nP(B) &= \\frac{1}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we construct the corresponding Venn diagram and shade the region $A'\\cup B'$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/4315/Source/Images/dfa6d853388443970cef0fa6c14c69db.png)\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nP(A'\\cup B') = \\dfrac1{3} + \\dfrac{1}{6} + \\dfrac{1}{3} = \\dfrac56\n$$"] [17592186198068 :question/problem "Given that $P(B)=0.6$, $P(A\\cap B)=0.4$, and $P(A\\cup B)=0.9$, find $P(A')$."] [17592186198068 :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $P(A)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(A∪B) &= P(A) + P(B) - P(A∩B) \\\\\n0.9 &= P(A) + 0.6 - 0.4 \\\\\nP(A) &= 0.9 + 0.4 - 0.6 \\\\\nP(A) &= 0.7\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(A^{′}) &= 1 - P(A) \\\\\n&= 1 - 0.7 \\\\\n&= 0.3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186232871] "immutable_fields" [[17592186197447 :answer-field/correct] [17592186197447 :answer-field/id] [17592186197447 :answer-field/key] [17592186197447 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
